  "id": "cardiac-neurosis",
  "term": "cardiac neurosis",
  "definition": "Cardiac neurosis refers to a syndrome in which slight physical effort brings on palpitations, shortness of breath, labored breathing, and a sense of strain or discomfort. It may also include dizziness, shakiness, sweating, and insomnia, and is commonly described as a form of anxiety disorder.",
